<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">Songs in History</h1><p class="ref-lede">126 songs that people have sung and handed down, in 61 languages, from a Sumerian hymn to the goddess of beer, copied about 1800 BCE, to songs of the last years of apartheid and of the Cold War. Each gives who made it, where and in what language, its story, what it says and the songs it led to. 78 carry their words: in the original and, for the songs not in English, romanized and translated line by line. 124 have a performance to listen to.</p></header>
